From: Kamil Bienkiewicz <perceivalpercy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: add the flow, host, nexthop 
 and L3 interface tables

The PPE routes and translates a flow in hardware from five tables: the
flow table (5-tuple and NAT overlay, hashed), the host table (the
address the flow entry points at), the nexthop table (egress port, tag
inserts, rewritten MAC and address), the public IP table (SNAT source),
and the L3 interface tables with MY_MAC and the port-to-L3-interface
binding. Add primitives for each, for the IPv4 layouts:

- table operations through the IPE_L3 indirect-op registers, stamping
  and matching a command ID so that a result is never taken from another
  operation, under a per-table lock;
- encoders for the IPv4 NAT flow entry (SNAT and DNAT overlays, source
  L3 interface, PMTU) and the IPv4 host entry;
- per-flow hit counters, read as deltas, cleared when an index is
  programmed;
- refcounted pools for host, nexthop and public IP entries, so that
  flows sharing one share the entry;
- the APPE register map of these tables (IPQ5332 builds as APPE/MPPE),
  the MY_MAC table and the port-to-L3-interface binding included.

Nothing calls them yet.

Ported from Kamil Bienkiewicz's flow offload series for the GL-BE9300
(perceival/openwrt-flint3 2365932733), his patches 0411-0418, 0421,
0431, 0433, 0434, 0436-0438, 0440 and 0441, the flow table base of 0454,
the @deacclr_en kernel-doc of 0442 and the table parts of 0450, 0451 and
0455, folded into their final state. Changes in the port: the IPv6 flow
and host layouts are left out (the IPv6 entry sizes stay, the table
operations taking either), the parser, TPID and exception registers move
to the patches that use them, and comments that pointed at IPv6 code or
at later patches are reworded; nothing else. His 0440 and 0441 carry no
Signed-off-by in his tree; this port carries none.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
